---
import ToolLayout from '../../layouts/ToolLayout.astro';
import CurlConverter from '../../components/CurlConverter.jsx';
---

<ToolLayout
  title="cURL to Code Converter"
  description="Paste a curl command and instantly get equivalent JavaScript (fetch) or Python (requests) code."
>
  <CurlConverter client:load slot="tool" />

  <h2>Why convert curl commands</h2>
  <p>
    API docs almost always show example requests as curl commands, but
    you're writing your integration in JavaScript or Python. Manually
    translating headers, methods, and JSON bodies is repetitive and easy to
    get wrong — this tool does it instantly, entirely in your browser.
  </p>

  <h2>How to use it</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Paste a curl command — from API docs, Postman, or your terminal history.</li>
    <li>Pick JavaScript or Python.</li>
    <li>Copy the generated code directly into your project.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>cURL Converter FAQ</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>Does this send my data anywhere?</strong> No — parsing happens
    entirely in your browser with JavaScript. Nothing is sent to a server.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Does it support every curl flag?</strong> It covers the most
    common flags (-X, -H, -d, and URL detection). Complex commands with file
    uploads or cookies may need manual adjustment.
  </p>
</ToolLayout>
